{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MpFodYa1NgnTewyBngBx1F","type":"tool_result","content":"src:\nassets.d.ts\nbuildinfo.ts\ncli/\ncli.ts\nconfig/\ncontext/\ncredentials/\nfsutil/\ngate/\ngit/\ngocompat/\nllm/\nprompts/\nrecord/\nrender/\nreview/\nrunbundle/\nscope/\nskill/\nsnapshot/\nstartup.ts\ntextsafe/\ntrust/\nutil/\nverify/\n\ntest/helpers:\nanthropic-fakes.ts\ndoctor-probe.ts\nenv.ts\ninference-server.ts\ninference-stream.ts\nprovider-server.ts\nrepo.ts\nreview.ts\nrun.ts\nspawn.ts\nstreams.ts\nterminal.ts\ntest.ts\n// The environment tests build `io.env` from (spec 01, 3.7).\n\nconst AMBIENT_PREFIXES = ['ANTHROPIC_', 'OPENAI_', 'OPENROUTER_', 'ROAST_']\n\n// A copy of `base` without any variable whose upper-cased name starts\n// with ANTHROPIC_, OPENAI_, OPENROUTER_, or ROAST_.\nexport function cleanEnv (\n    base:Readonly<Record<string, string|undefined>>\n):Record<string, string> {\n    const env:Record<string, string> = {}\n    for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(base)) {\n        if (value === undefined) continue\n        const upper = key.toUpperCase()\n        if (AMBIENT_PREFIXES.some(p => upper.startsWith(p))) continue\n        env[key] = value\n    }\n    return env\n}\n# Stored credentials, login, logout\n\nGo: `internal/credentials`, `internal/cli/login.go`,\n`internal/cli/openrouter_login.go`, `internal/cli/logout.go`.\nTS: `src/credentials/`. Design: ADR-0002.\n\n## Resolution order\n\n- `ROAST_<ROLE>_API_KEY`, then a profile's `api_key_env`, then\n  `OPENAI_API_KEY` / `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, then stored credentials; the\n  last three only at that provider's built-in endpoint.\n- Initial resolution (`resolveCredential`) and override rebinding\n  (`rebindCredential`) must agree: both reach the provider variable and\n  stored key through `ambientCredential`, so a role picks the same\n  credential with or without a same-provider protocol override. Keep\n  `DescribeCredential` in step with any change to that order.\n\n## Store\n\n- Project scope is `<git-common-dir>/roast/credentials.json`\n  (`trust.StateDir`, shared with `trust.json`); user scope is\n  `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/roast/credentials.json`, else\n  `~/.config/roast/credentials.json`.\n- Go `config` cannot import `credentials` (it validates provider names\n  through `config.LookupProvider`), so `config.StoredCredentials` is an\n  interface. The CLI attaches `credentials.NewStore(\".\")` with\n  `withStoredCredentials` (`internal/cli/config.go`); any new path that\n  resolves roles from a `config.Load` result must attach it too, or\n  stored keys are silently unused. `ResolvedRole` carries the store so\n  `OverrideEndpoint` can rebind.\n- TS `loadProjectConfig` attaches `openCredentialStore(ctx.cwd,\n  ctx.env)`. `CredentialStore.lookup` is synchronous (roles resolve\n  synchronously), so the async open resolves both scope paths up front\n  and lookup reads files lazily with sync `fs`, caching only successful\n  loads. Decode with the strict zod schema but read the validated input,\n  as `config/load.ts` does.\n- Files are read lazily: a bad file fails resolution only when a role\n  reaches it (no env credential first). `roast doctor` also loads each\n  scope's file that exists (`doctorStoredCredentialChecks`, results\n  `project-credentials` / `user-credentials`), so a broken file fails\n  doctor even when env credentials shadow it. Doctor reads the\n  user-scope file too, so a doctor test that expects a clean exit\n  isolates `HOME`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Go: chdir into a temp Git repository (the project file lands in its\n  `.git`) and isolate `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`\n  (`isolateCredentialHome`, `stored_credentials_test.go`).\n  `storedCredentialRepo` swaps `http.DefaultTransport`, so call it at\n  most once per test or subtest; loop over cases with `t.Run`.\n  `storeKeys` (`logout_test.go`) seeds several providers.\n- TS: put files at `<repo>/.git/roast/credentials.json` and\n  `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/roast/credentials.json` from `tempRepo().env`.\n\n## Login and logout (Go)\n\n- Browser opening goes through the package var `openBrowser`\n  (`internal/cli/prompt.go`, takes a URL). Tests swap it with\n  `captureBrowser(t)` (`login_test.go`), which returns the URLs it was\n  asked to open. Login prints every URL too, so a failing opener never\n  blocks it.\n- `readSecret` reads without echo only on a real terminal; with test\n  stdin it reads plain lines from one `bufio.Reader` kept across\n  retries, so tests pass several answers as `\"key1\\nkey2\\n\"`.\n- A command that prompts and then reads keys passes one `*bufio.Reader`\n  to both `promptYesDefault` and `loginProvider`; a fresh reader per\n  prompt swallows the buffered answers that tests feed as one string.\n- `login` with no argument and `init`'s login offer share\n  `providersNeedingLogin` (built-in providers of roles that resolve no\n  credential) and `loginProvider` (one provider, given scope path).\n- `logout` shares `loginPath` (scope and the outside-a-repository usage\n  error) and `providerNames` with login; keep scope rules in that one\n  helper.\n- `providerServer` (`init_test.go`) answers `GET /v1/models` for key\n  validation; `answerModels` sets the status per credential. With\n  `redirectDefaultTransport`, login's validation request reaches it.\n  `loginRepo(t)` (`login_test.go`) sets up repo, fake, terminal, and\n  opener in one call; `initLoginRepo(t, terminals)` (`init_test.go`)\n  does the same for init.\n- OpenRouter login is a PKCE exchange: the fake mints\n  `sk-or-minted-<code>` at `POST /api/v1/auth/keys` and checks keys at\n  `GET /api/v1/key` (`answerKey`). Tests run login in the background\n  (`startRoast`), read the opened URL (`awaitOpened`), and hit its\n  `callback_url` with `callOpenRouterBack`, which uses its own transport\n  because `redirectDefaultTransport` would send loopback requests to\n  the fake. Any test that might wait for a callback shortens the wait\n  with `shortBrowserTimeout`, so a regression fails fast instead of\n  hanging for five minutes.\n# Trust\n\nGo: `internal/config/trust.go`, `internal/trust`, `internal/cli/trust.go`.\nTS: `src/config/trust.ts`, `src/config/canonical.ts`,\n`src/trust/trust.ts`, `src/cli/trust.ts`. Design: ADR-0001, ADR-0003.\nHow CLI tests approve a config is in `go.md`.\n\n- `Config.TrustProjection()` is the security-relevant projection; its\n  `Hash()` covers only endpoint, protocol, credential variable, and\n  prompt-override paths. A new security-relevant config field goes into\n  the projection, or it can change without re-approval.\n- Approvals live in `<git-common-dir>/roast/trust.json`. `roast review`\n  calls `requireTrust` before building scope; untrusted is a usage error\n  (exit 2), never `ExitFindings`.\n- TS `src/config/trust.ts` (projection, `requiresApproval`, hash v2) is\n  pure. `src/config/canonical.ts` is the only JSON canonicalizer; its\n  input types must be `type` aliases, not interfaces, to be assignable\n  to `CanonicalValue`.\n- TS `src/trust/trust.ts` takes a trailing `{signal, env}` for git.\n  `src/cli/trust.ts` has the command, `writeTrustSummary` (every value\n  through `textsafe.line`) and `requireTrust(dir, cfg, io)`.\n  `promptNoDefault` (`[y/N]`) lives in `src/cli/terminal.ts`.\n# Run records\n\nGo: `internal/record`, `internal/cli/ignore.go`.\n\n- `record.DefaultDir()` is `.roast/runs` at the Git toplevel of the\n  process working directory (`\"\"` outside a repository); there is no env\n  override. Run directories are `<DefaultDir>/<run-id>/`; the monthly\n  JSONL index is `<DefaultDir>/runs-YYYY-MM.jsonl`.\n- A test that writes or reads records `t.Chdir`s into a temporary Git\n  repository first (`useProject` in `internal/record/record_test.go`).\n- `roast ignore` (`ensureStateIgnored`) owns the toplevel `/.roast/`\n  entry; reuse it rather than writing `.gitignore` again.\n\nTS (`src/cli/runs.ts`):\n\n- `runs` lists the monthly index; `runsSubcommands` is the array the\n  snapshot area appends `checkout` and `prune` to. Run IDs go through\n  `reportPath` / `resolveRunDir`, which own the plain-name check, so\n  CLI code never joins an ID into a path itself.\n- CLI tests fabricate records with `writeReport` and raw writes to\n  `.roast/runs/runs-YYYY-MM.jsonl` inside `recordRepo`; no review needed.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc9cd1ee-6217-41cc-8c13-e5fed07b92d5","uuid":"c30aaf09-0c74-4c43-a20b-c0e28b950fc6","timestamp":"2026-11-24T03:52:00.847Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"src:\nassets.d.ts\nbuildinfo.ts\ncli/\ncli.ts\nconfig/\ncontext/\ncredentials/\nfsutil/\ngate/\ngit/\ngocompat/\nllm/\nprompts/\nrecord/\nrender/\nreview/\nrunbundle/\nscope/\nskill/\nsnapshot/\nstartup.ts\ntextsafe/\ntrust/\nutil/\nverify/\n\ntest/helpers:\nanthropic-fakes.ts\ndoctor-probe.ts\nenv.ts\ninference-server.ts\ninference-stream.ts\nprovider-server.ts\nrepo.ts\nreview.ts\nrun.ts\nspawn.ts\nstreams.ts\nterminal.ts\ntest.ts\n// The environment tests build `io.env` from (spec 01, 3.7).\n\nconst AMBIENT_PREFIXES = ['ANTHROPIC_', 'OPENAI_', 'OPENROUTER_', 'ROAST_']\n\n// A copy of `base` without any variable whose upper-cased name starts\n// with ANTHROPIC_, OPENAI_, OPENROUTER_, or ROAST_.\nexport function cleanEnv (\n    base:Readonly<Record<string, string|undefined>>\n):Record<string, string> {\n    const env:Record<string, string> = {}\n    for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(base)) {\n        if (value === undefined) continue\n        const upper = key.toUpperCase()\n        if (AMBIENT_PREFIXES.some(p => upper.startsWith(p))) continue\n        env[key] = value\n    }\n    return env\n}\n# Stored credentials, login, logout\n\nGo: `internal/credentials`, `internal/cli/login.go`,\n`internal/cli/openrouter_login.go`, `internal/cli/logout.go`.\nTS: `src/credentials/`. Design: ADR-0002.\n\n## Resolution order\n\n- `ROAST_<ROLE>_API_KEY`, then a profile's `api_key_env`, then\n  `OPENAI_API_KEY` / `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, then stored credentials; the\n  last three only at that provider's built-in endpoint.\n- Initial resolution (`resolveCredential`) and override rebinding\n  (`rebindCredential`) must agree: both reach the provider variable and\n  stored key through `ambientCredential`, so a role picks the same\n  credential with or without a same-provider protocol override. Keep\n  `DescribeCredential` in step with any change to that order.\n\n## Store\n\n- Project scope is `<git-common-dir>/roast/credentials.json`\n  (`trust.StateDir`, shared with `trust.json`); user scope is\n  `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/roast/credentials.json`, else\n  `~/.config/roast/credentials.json`.\n- Go `config` cannot import `credentials` (it validates provider names\n  through `config.LookupProvider`), so `config.StoredCredentials` is an\n  interface. The CLI attaches `credentials.NewStore(\".\")` with\n  `withStoredCredentials` (`internal/cli/config.go`); any new path that\n  resolves roles from a `config.Load` result must attach it too, or\n  stored keys are silently unused. `ResolvedRole` carries the store so\n  `OverrideEndpoint` can rebind.\n- TS `loadProjectConfig` attaches `openCredentialStore(ctx.cwd,\n  ctx.env)`. `CredentialStore.lookup` is synchronous (roles resolve\n  synchronously), so the async open resolves both scope paths up front\n  and lookup reads files lazily with sync `fs`, caching only successful\n  loads. Decode with the strict zod schema but read the validated input,\n  as `config/load.ts` does.\n- Files are read lazily: a bad file fails resolution only when a role\n  reaches it (no env credential first). `roast doctor` also loads each\n  scope's file that exists (`doctorStoredCredentialChecks`, results\n  `project-credentials` / `user-credentials`), so a broken file fails\n  doctor even when env credentials shadow it. Doctor reads the\n  user-scope file too, so a doctor test that expects a clean exit\n  isolates `HOME`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Go: chdir into a temp Git repository (the project file lands in its\n  `.git`) and isolate `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`\n  (`isolateCredentialHome`, `stored_credentials_test.go`).\n  `storedCredentialRepo` swaps `http.DefaultTransport`, so call it at\n  most once per test or subtest; loop over cases with `t.Run`.\n  `storeKeys` (`logout_test.go`) seeds several providers.\n- TS: put files at `<repo>/.git/roast/credentials.json` and\n  `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/roast/credentials.json` from `tempRepo().env`.\n\n## Login and logout (Go)\n\n- Browser opening goes through the package var `openBrowser`\n  (`internal/cli/prompt.go`, takes a URL). Tests swap it with\n  `captureBrowser(t)` (`login_test.go`), which returns the URLs it was\n  asked to open. Login prints every URL too, so a failing opener never\n  blocks it.\n- `readSecret` reads without echo only on a real terminal; with test\n  stdin it reads plain lines from one `bufio.Reader` kept across\n  retries, so tests pass several answers as `\"key1\\nkey2\\n\"`.\n- A command that prompts and then reads keys passes one `*bufio.Reader`\n  to both `promptYesDefault` and `loginProvider`; a fresh reader per\n  prompt swallows the buffered answers that tests feed as one string.\n- `login` with no argument and `init`'s login offer share\n  `providersNeedingLogin` (built-in providers of roles that resolve no\n  credential) and `loginProvider` (one provider, given scope path).\n- `logout` shares `loginPath` (scope and the outside-a-repository usage\n  error) and `providerNames` with login; keep scope rules in that one\n  helper.\n- `providerServer` (`init_test.go`) answers `GET /v1/models` for key\n  validation; `answerModels` sets the status per credential. With\n  `redirectDefaultTransport`, login's validation request reaches it.\n  `loginRepo(t)` (`login_test.go`) sets up repo, fake, terminal, and\n  opener in one call; `initLoginRepo(t, terminals)` (`init_test.go`)\n  does the same for init.\n- OpenRouter login is a PKCE exchange: the fake mints\n  `sk-or-minted-<code>` at `POST /api/v1/auth/keys` and checks keys at\n  `GET /api/v1/key` (`answerKey`). Tests run login in the background\n  (`startRoast`), read the opened URL (`awaitOpened`), and hit its\n  `callback_url` with `callOpenRouterBack`, which uses its own transport\n  because `redirectDefaultTransport` would send loopback requests to\n  the fake. Any test that might wait for a callback shortens the wait\n  with `shortBrowserTimeout`, so a regression fails fast instead of\n  hanging for five minutes.\n# Trust\n\nGo: `internal/config/trust.go`, `internal/trust`, `internal/cli/trust.go`.\nTS: `src/config/trust.ts`, `src/config/canonical.ts`,\n`src/trust/trust.ts`, `src/cli/trust.ts`. Design: ADR-0001, ADR-0003.\nHow CLI tests approve a config is in `go.md`.\n\n- `Config.TrustProjection()` is the security-relevant projection; its\n  `Hash()` covers only endpoint, protocol, credential variable, and\n  prompt-override paths. A new security-relevant config field goes into\n  the projection, or it can change without re-approval.\n- Approvals live in `<git-common-dir>/roast/trust.json`. `roast review`\n  calls `requireTrust` before building scope; untrusted is a usage error\n  (exit 2), never `ExitFindings`.\n- TS `src/config/trust.ts` (projection, `requiresApproval`, hash v2) is\n  pure. `src/config/canonical.ts` is the only JSON canonicalizer; its\n  input types must be `type` aliases, not interfaces, to be assignable\n  to `CanonicalValue`.\n- TS `src/trust/trust.ts` takes a trailing `{signal, env}` for git.\n  `src/cli/trust.ts` has the command, `writeTrustSummary` (every value\n  through `textsafe.line`) and `requireTrust(dir, cfg, io)`.\n  `promptNoDefault` (`[y/N]`) lives in `src/cli/terminal.ts`.\n# Run records\n\nGo: `internal/record`, `internal/cli/ignore.go`.\n\n- `record.DefaultDir()` is `.roast/runs` at the Git toplevel of the\n  process working directory (`\"\"` outside a repository); there is no env\n  override. Run directories are `<DefaultDir>/<run-id>/`; the monthly\n  JSONL