{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JHkTBiniTs4BkAVAnWz85d","type":"tool_result","content":"src/prompts/AGENTS.md:3:- Import shared system templates from `internal/prompts/templates/`\nsrc/prompts/AGENTS.md:22:- Until M6, `npm run test:diff` compares user prompt bytes with the Go\n# Config, roles, and providers\n\nGo: `internal/config`, `internal/cli/config.go`. TS: `src/config/`,\n`src/cli/config.ts`. Credential lookup order is in `auth.md`.\n\n## Loading\n\n- Go `config.Load(path)` parses `.roast.json` as JSONC\n  (`hujson.Standardize`, then `encoding/json` with\n  `DisallowUnknownFields`). `version: 1` is required; a literal\n  `api_key` is rejected. There are no built-in roles or models: a role\n  missing from the config fails in `ResolveRole`.\n- TS `jsonc.ts` parses into null-prototype objects (`newObject` /\n  `setKey`, so `__proto__` is an ordinary key). `schema.ts` (zod) checks\n  shape and types only, and `load.ts` keeps the validated *input*, never\n  zod's output (zod's record output turns a `__proto__` key into a\n  prototype). Range and cross-field checks are plain functions in\n  `load.ts` so Go's check order holds.\n- `config.Find(start, stop)` walks up to `stop` (the Git toplevel),\n  comparing directories after `EvalSymlinks`: macOS temp dirs are\n  `/var/...` while `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` prints\n  `/private/var/...`.\n- The CLI loads config only through `loadProjectConfig` (Go also\n  `projectConfigPath`; TS `loadProjectConfig(explicit, ctx)`), which\n  attaches the stored-credentials store. A missing config is a usage\n  error naming `npx roast init`.\n- Relative prompt-override paths resolve against the config file's\n  directory: `config.Load` records it and callers read prompts through\n  `cfg.PromptPath(...)`, never the raw `cfg.Prompts.*` string. The trust\n  projection hashes the raw string, so approvals survive worktree moves.\n\n## Settings\n\nOnly credentials come from outside the config. Every other setting is\nin it (`limits`, `interactive`, `gate`, `review.snapshot`); optional\nnumbers are pointers so an explicit 0 differs from unset, and\n`validateSettings` checks ranges. Go `cli.go` resolves them with\n`flagOrConfigInt` / `flagOrConfigDuration` (flag, then config, then\ndefault).\n\n## Schema and starter\n\n- `roast.schema.json` (repo root, shipped through `package.json`\n  `files`) is generated: `npm run schema` renders\n  `src/config/json-schema.ts` from the zod schema. Adding, removing, or\n  retyping a config field changes `config.Config` and the zod schema in\n  the same change, then regenerates; never edit the JSON by hand.\n  `TestSchemaMatchesConfigStruct` (Go) and `test/config/schema.ts` fail\n  on drift. Editor-only constraints (enum, pattern, minimum, required)\n  go in the zod `.meta()`.\n- The `roast init` starter (`internal/config/starter.go`) shows\n  commented-out defaults that must track the defaults in\n  `internal/cli/cli.go`.\n- The starter places a model by its ID alone (`placeModel`): a\n  `<vendor>/<model>[:<variant>]` ID goes to OpenRouter, a bare ID to the\n  provider `InferFamily` names. A placeholder role follows an OpenRouter\n  role onto OpenRouter; otherwise it takes the other direct provider.\n\n## Providers\n\n- `LookupProvider(name)` and `ProviderAt(endpoint, protocol)`\n  (`internal/config/provider.go`) are the one place that says which\n  endpoint, protocols, standard key variable, key page, and login method\n  a provider has. Trust standardness, ambient credentials, and the\n  `init` starter consult it; add a provider there, not in those callers.\n  A provider's first protocol is the one starter profiles use.\n- A new provider's key variable also goes in `clearProviderEnv`\n  (`internal/config/credential_test.go`).\n- `DefaultBaseURL(protocol)` stays separate: it is the implicit endpoint\n  of a profile that omits one; OpenRouter is never one.\n- A role that gets no ambient key reports any set provider key variable\n  as `Withheld` (`withheldKey`), preferring the protocol's default\n  provider.\n- TS `provider.ts` `parseEndpoint` is the one endpoint parser (treats\n  `https:///v1` and `https:v1` as an empty host, like Go); `endpoint.ts`\n  and `sameEndpoint` use it.\n\n## TS roles (`role.ts`, `credential.ts`, `provider.ts`)\n\n- Resolution takes `env` explicitly and never reads `process.env`.\n- `ResolvedRole` is frozen with a non-enumerable `apiKey` and `stored`,\n  so JSON, spread, and `util.inspect` omit the secret. Change a role\n  with `updateRole(role, changes)`; a `{...role}` spread drops the key.\n- `StoredCredentials` lives in `credential.ts` (re-exported by\n  `load.ts`).\n\n## TS tests\n\n- Role tests build configs with `configFrom` / `resolveFinder` and the\n  in-memory `FakeStore` in `test/config/helpers.ts`.\n- Configs the tests load as realistic examples go in\n  `test/config/examples.ts`; the schema test validates each with ajv.\n# Gate\n\nGo: `internal/gate`, `internal/cli/gate.go`. TS: `src/gate/`.\n\n## Hook behavior\n\n- The hook (`internal/gate/pre-commit.sh`, embedded as `HookScript`)\n  runs only `node_modules/.bin/roast` at the Git toplevel, never `PATH`.\n  It first calls the hidden `roast gate settings` (prints\n  `timeout_seconds=` and `severity=` lines from the config's `gate`\n  section, defaults 180/HIGH), then `roast review --staged ...\n  --max-severity <severity>`. Any failure, including a settings query\n  that exits non-zero, warns and allows the commit; only review exit 1\n  blocks.\n- The hook runs from the Git toplevel without `--config`, so it sees\n  only a toplevel `.roast.json` (`gateConfigPath` in\n  `internal/cli/config.go`). `gate enable` refuses and the review-time\n  bootstrap stays silent without one; `gate enable` tests write a\n  toplevel config first.\n- Installed hooks are refreshed by content comparison with the script,\n  so editing it needs no version bump.\n- TS `HOOK_SCRIPT` is `internal/gate/pre-commit.sh` through the text\n  loader (byte-identical, so Go-installed hooks are not stale).\n  `hook.ts` handles hook bodies as `Buffer`s so strip keeps every\n  foreign byte. Hook writes use `fsutil` `writeFileAtomic` with `mode`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Go hook execution tests (`hook_exec_test.go`) drive a real\n  `git commit` with a shell stub that `newStub(t, repo...)` writes at\n  each repo's `node_modules/.bin/roast`. It answers `gate settings` from\n  `STUB_TIMEOUT` / `STUB_SEVERITY` and logs only the review call\n  (`ARGS:` plus the staged diff), so `stub.ran` is empty when no review\n  happened.\n- TS gate tests build repos with `gateRepo(t)` (`test/gate/helpers.ts`:\n  global/system git config cut out, maintenance off, toplevel\n  `.roast.json`); hook execution tests use `seededRepo`, `newStub`, and\n  `commit` from `test/gate/exec-helpers.ts`.\n- Simulate a non-local `roast.gate` with\n  `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`/`KEY_0`/`VALUE_0`, never a global file.\n- `ROAST_TEST_SKIP_GATE_TIMEOUT=1` skips the sleeping tests.\n- The review-time offer (`src/cli/gate-offer.ts`, `src/gate/bootstrap.ts`)\n  runs at the start of every `review` / bare `roast` with a toplevel\n  config. Without terminals it records `roast.gate-notice=sent`; with\n  `simulateTerminals(t, true)` it reads the first stdin line. A review\n  test that feeds stdin to a later prompt (trust, keys) must first record\n  `roast.gate` or set `gate.offer: false`, or account for the offer\n  taking that line. Offer tests are in `test/cli/gate-offer.ts`.\n# Agent skill install\n\nGo: `internal/skill`, `internal/cli/skill.go`. TS: `src/skill/`.\n\n- `skill.InstallationTargets(parent, projectRoot)` resolves targets: a\n  non-empty `parent` (`--dir`) wins, then a non-empty `projectRoot`\n  gives project-local targets, otherwise the user-level targets. The CLI\n  maps `--dir`, `--global`, and the Git toplevel onto it; `doctor`\n  inspects user-level targets.\n- The bundled skill text in `internal/skill/assets/roast/SKILL.md`\n  describes the install locations; update it when target resolution\n  changes.\n- TS `src/skill/assets.ts` imports each file under\n  `internal/skill/assets/roast/` explicitly; a new file there needs a\n  new import, and `test/skill/assets.ts` fails until it has one.\n- TS reads home, `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, and `PATH` from\n  the context env. `skillHooks.lookPath` is the swappable lookup.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Tests isolate `HOME`, `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` so\n  they can assert nothing reaches the real user directories:\n  `isolateSkillHome` in `internal/cli/skill_test.go` (Go) and\n  `test/cli/skill.ts` (TS). Keep `PATH`: the CLI shells out to `git`.\n- The TS `isolateSkillHome` blanks the two config overrides, because\n  `isolatedEnv` sets `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, which counts as Claude Code\n  being present.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc9cd1ee-6217-41cc-8c13-e5fed07b92d5","uuid":"c774f73b-54fb-49ae-a108-5c9c31c09680","timestamp":"2026-11-24T03:52:11.505Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"src/prompts/AGENTS.md:3:- Import shared system templates from `internal/prompts/templates/`\nsrc/prompts/AGENTS.md:22:- Until M6, `npm run test:diff` compares user prompt bytes with the Go\n# Config, roles, and providers\n\nGo: `internal/config`, `internal/cli/config.go`. TS: `src/config/`,\n`src/cli/config.ts`. Credential lookup order is in `auth.md`.\n\n## Loading\n\n- Go `config.Load(path)` parses `.roast.json` as JSONC\n  (`hujson.Standardize`, then `encoding/json` with\n  `DisallowUnknownFields`). `version: 1` is required; a literal\n  `api_key` is rejected. There are no built-in roles or models: a role\n  missing from the config fails in `ResolveRole`.\n- TS `jsonc.ts` parses into null-prototype objects (`newObject` /\n  `setKey`, so `__proto__` is an ordinary key). `schema.ts` (zod) checks\n  shape and types only, and `load.ts` keeps the validated *input*, never\n  zod's output (zod's record output turns a `__proto__` key into a\n  prototype). Range and cross-field checks are plain functions in\n  `load.ts` so Go's check order holds.\n- `config.Find(start, stop)` walks up to `stop` (the Git toplevel),\n  comparing directories after `EvalSymlinks`: macOS temp dirs are\n  `/var/...` while `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` prints\n  `/private/var/...`.\n- The CLI loads config only through `loadProjectConfig` (Go also\n  `projectConfigPath`; TS `loadProjectConfig(explicit, ctx)`), which\n  attaches the stored-credentials store. A missing config is a usage\n  error naming `npx roast init`.\n- Relative prompt-override paths resolve against the config file's\n  directory: `config.Load` records it and callers read prompts through\n  `cfg.PromptPath(...)`, never the raw `cfg.Prompts.*` string. The trust\n  projection hashes the raw string, so approvals survive worktree moves.\n\n## Settings\n\nOnly credentials come from outside the config. Every other setting is\nin it (`limits`, `interactive`, `gate`, `review.snapshot`); optional\nnumbers are pointers so an explicit 0 differs from unset, and\n`validateSettings` checks ranges. Go `cli.go` resolves them with\n`flagOrConfigInt` / `flagOrConfigDuration` (flag, then config, then\ndefault).\n\n## Schema and starter\n\n- `roast.schema.json` (repo root, shipped through `package.json`\n  `files`) is generated: `npm run schema` renders\n  `src/config/json-schema.ts` from the zod schema. Adding, removing, or\n  retyping a config field changes `config.Config` and the zod schema in\n  the same change, then regenerates; never edit the JSON by hand.\n  `TestSchemaMatchesConfigStruct` (Go) and `test/config/schema.ts` fail\n  on drift. Editor-only constraints (enum, pattern, minimum, required)\n  go in the zod `.meta()`.\n- The `roast init` starter (`internal/config/starter.go`) shows\n  commented-out defaults that must track the defaults in\n  `internal/cli/cli.go`.\n- The starter places a model by its ID alone (`placeModel`): a\n  `<vendor>/<model>[:<variant>]` ID goes to OpenRouter, a bare ID to the\n  provider `InferFamily` names. A placeholder role follows an OpenRouter\n  role onto OpenRouter; otherwise it takes the other direct provider.\n\n## Providers\n\n- `LookupProvider(name)` and `ProviderAt(endpoint, protocol)`\n  (`internal/config/provider.go`) are the one place that says which\n  endpoint, protocols, standard key variable, key page, and login method\n  a provider has. Trust standardness, ambient credentials, and the\n  `init` starter consult it; add a provider there, not in those callers.\n  A provider's first protocol is the one starter profiles use.\n- A new provider's key variable also goes in `clearProviderEnv`\n  (`internal/config/credential_test.go`).\n- `DefaultBaseURL(protocol)` stays separate: it is the implicit endpoint\n  of a profile that omits one; OpenRouter is never one.\n- A role that gets no ambient key reports any set provider key variable\n  as `Withheld` (`withheldKey`), preferring the protocol's default\n  provider.\n- TS `provider.ts` `parseEndpoint` is the one endpoint parser (treats\n  `https:///v1` and `https:v1` as an empty host, like Go); `endpoint.ts`\n  and `sameEndpoint` use it.\n\n## TS roles (`role.ts`, `credential.ts`, `provider.ts`)\n\n- Resolution takes `env` explicitly and never reads `process.env`.\n- `ResolvedRole` is frozen with a non-enumerable `apiKey` and `stored`,\n  so JSON, spread, and `util.inspect` omit the secret. Change a role\n  with `updateRole(role, changes)`; a `{...role}` spread drops the key.\n- `StoredCredentials` lives in `credential.ts` (re-exported by\n  `load.ts`).\n\n## TS tests\n\n- Role tests build configs with `configFrom` / `resolveFinder` and the\n  in-memory `FakeStore` in `test/config/helpers.ts`.\n- Configs the tests load as realistic examples go in\n  `test/config/examples.ts`; the schema test validates each with ajv.\n# Gate\n\nGo: `internal/gate`, `internal/cli/gate.go`. TS: `src/gate/`.\n\n## Hook behavior\n\n- The hook (`internal/gate/pre-commit.sh`, embedded as `HookScript`)\n  runs only `node_modules/.bin/roast` at the Git toplevel, never `PATH`.\n  It first calls the hidden `roast gate settings` (prints\n  `timeout_seconds=` and `severity=` lines from the config's `gate`\n  section, defaults 180/HIGH), then `roast review --staged ...\n  --max-severity <severity>`. Any failure, including a settings query\n  that exits non-zero, warns and allows the commit; only review exit 1\n  blocks.\n- The hook runs from the Git toplevel without `--config`, so it sees\n  only a toplevel `.roast.json` (`gateConfigPath` in\n  `internal/cli/config.go`). `gate enable` refuses and the review-time\n  bootstrap stays silent without one; `gate enable` tests write a\n  toplevel config first.\n- Installed hooks are refreshed by content comparison with the script,\n  so editing it needs no version bump.\n- TS `HOOK_SCRIPT` is `internal/gate/pre-commit.sh` through the text\n  loader (byte-identical, so Go-installed hooks are not stale).\n  `hook.ts` handles hook bodies as `Buffer`s so strip keeps every\n  foreign byte. Hook writes use `fsutil` `writeFileAtomic` with `mode`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Go hook execution tests (`hook_exec_test.go`) drive a real\n  `git commit` with a shell stub that `newStub(t, repo...)` writes at\n  each repo's `node_modules/.bin/roast`. It answers `gate settings` from\n  `STUB_TIMEOUT` / `STUB_SEVERITY` and logs only the review call\n  (`ARGS:` plus the staged diff), so `stub.ran` is empty when no review\n  happened.\n- TS gate tests build repos with `gateRepo(t)` (`test/gate/helpers.ts`:\n  global/system git config cut out, maintenance off, toplevel\n  `.roast.json`); hook execution tests use `seededRepo`, `newStub`, and\n  `commit` from `test/gate/exec-helpers.ts`.\n- Simulate a non-local `roast.gate` with\n  `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`/`KEY_0`/`VALUE_0`, never a global file.\n- `ROAST_TEST_SKIP_GATE_TIMEOUT=1` skips the sleeping tests.\n- The review-time offer (`src/cli/gate-offer.ts`, `src/gate/bootstrap.ts`)\n  runs at the start of every `review` / bare `roast` with a toplevel\n  config. Without terminals it records `roast.gate-notice=sent`; with\n  `simulateTerminals(t, true)` it reads the first stdin line. A review\n  test that feeds stdin to a later prompt (trust, keys) must first record\n  `roast.gate` or set `gate.offer: false`, or account for the offer\n  taking that line. Offer tests are in `test/cli/gate-offer.ts`.\n# Agent skill install\n\nGo: `internal/skill`, `internal/cli/skill.go`. TS: `src/skill/`.\n\n- `skill.InstallationTargets(parent, projectRoot)` resolves targets: a\n  non-empty `parent` (`--dir`) wins, then a non-empty `projectRoot`\n  gives project-local targets, otherwise the user-level targets. The CLI\n  maps `--dir`, `--global`, and the Git toplevel onto it; `doctor`\n  inspects user-level targets.\n- The bundled skill text in `internal/skill/assets/roast/SKILL.md`\n  describes the install locations; update it when target resolution\n  changes.\n- TS `src/skill/assets.ts` imports each file under\n  `internal/skill/assets/roast/` explicitly; a new file there needs a\n  new import, and `test/skill/assets.ts` fails until it has one.\n- TS reads home, `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, and `PATH` from\n  the context env. `skillHooks.lookPath` is the swappable lookup.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Tests isolate `HOME`, `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` so\n  they can assert nothing reaches the real user directories:\n  `isolateSkillHome` in `internal/cli/skill_test.go` (Go) and\n  `test/cli/skill.ts` (TS). Keep `PATH`: the CLI shells out to `git`.\n- The TS `isolateSkillHome` blanks the two config overrides, because\n  `isolatedEnv` sets `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, which counts as Claude Code\n  being present.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JHkTBiniTs4BkAVAnWz85d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
