{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0154CLWsasdoN8zvhLj6aJYh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Agent skills\n2\t\n3\t### Issue tracker\n4\t\n5\tIssues are tracked as local markdown files under `.scratch/`. See `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.\n6\t\n7\t### Triage labels\n8\t\n9\tDefault label vocabulary. See `docs/agents/triage-labels.md`.\n10\t\n11\t### Domain docs\n12\t\n13\tSingle-context layout. See `docs/agents/domain.md`.\n14\t\n15\t## Layout\n16\t\n17\tTwo implementations live side by side until the M6 cutover\n18\t(`.scratch/ts-rewrite/`, ADR-0004): the Go CLI (`cmd/roast`,\n19\t`internal/`) and its TypeScript rewrite (`src/`, `test/`, `scripts/`).\n20\tBoth are under active change. `npm run test:go` runs the Go and launcher\n21\ttests; `npm test` runs typecheck and the TS suite; lint is\n22\t`npm run lint`.\n23\t\n24\t## Area notes\n25\t\n26\tBefore editing code in an area, read its notes. Each area file holds the\n27\tGo and TS notes for that area side by side.\n28\t\n29\t- Any Go code or Go test: `docs/agents/go.md`\n30\t- Any TS in `src/`, `test/`, or `scripts/`: `docs/agents/typescript.md`\n31\t- Config loading, roles, providers, the `init` starter,\n32\t  `roast.schema.json` (`internal/config`, `src/config/`):\n33\t  `docs/agents/config.md`\n34\t- Trust and approvals (`internal/trust`, `src/trust/`, `*/trust.*`):\n35\t  `docs/agents/trust.md`\n36\t- Stored credentials, `login`, `logout` (`internal/credentials`,\n37\t  `src/credentials/`, `internal/cli/*login*`): `docs/agents/auth.md`\n38\t- Gate and the pre-commit hook (`internal/gate`, `src/gate/`):\n39\t  `docs/agents/gate.md`\n40\t- Agent skill install (`internal/skill`, `src/skill/`):\n41\t  `docs/agents/skill.md`\n42\t- Run records (`internal/record`): `docs/agents/records.md`\n43\t- Scope, context, exploration tools, snapshot denylist (`src/scope/`,\n44\t  `src/context/`, `src/snapshot/`): `docs/agents/scope-context.md`\n45\t- LLM adapters and the agent loop (`src/llm/`): `docs/agents/llm.md`\n46\t- npm packaging, the launcher, release (`packages/`, `scripts/build.ts`,\n47\t  `src/launcher.ts`): `docs/agents/packaging.md`\n48\t\n49\tA new note goes in its area's file; a new area gets a file and a line\n50\there. This file holds only what most tasks hit.\n51\t\n52\t## Traps every task hits\n53\t\n54\t- `JSON.parse` syntax errors can quote the input. Credential-file parse\n55\t  errors must use value-free messages so diagnostic output cannot expose\n56\t  a stored key.\n57\t- Shell hooks block Bash commands that contain a heredoc mentioning\n58\t  `process.env.PATH`, a heredoc or command containing `env:` or `.env`\n59\t  text, or a `credentials*` path together with `cat`, `sed`, `head`, and\n60\t  the like. Read and write such files with the editor tools.\n61\t- Tests that write project state (run records, trust, stored\n62\t  credentials) chdir into a temporary Git repository first. `.roast/`\n63\t  ignores itself, so a leak into this checkout is invisible to\n64\t  `git status`; check with `ls -a`.\n65\t- CLI diagnostic tests that resolve roles need valid test credentials\n66\t  and local fake-server routing, even when asserting only local checks.\n67\t  Doctor fakes must route GET models checks and POST inference separately;\n68\t  a successful chat probe needs a lookup call followed by a final call\n69\t  that echoes the token from the replayed tool result.\n70\t- `.npmrc` sets `force=true` so npm links workspaces whose `os`/`cpu`\n71\t  differ from the host. Expect \"using --force\" warnings from every npm\n72\t  command.\n73\t- The CLI parser preserves dashed option names and disables boolean\n74\t  negation. Declare flags such as `no-browser` explicitly and read\n75\t  `args['no-browser']`, rather than a camel-case property.\n76\t- `simulateTerminals` only bypasses interactive-terminal detection. To\n77\t  exercise raw-mode prompt input through the CLI, give stdin an `isTTY`\n78\t  value of `true` and a `setRawMode` function; assert raw mode is restored.\n79\t- Browser-login tests send callbacks with the real fetch; the injected\n80\t  provider fetch rewrites every origin. Bound callback tests with\n81\t  `loginTimeouts.browser` and set injected display variables on Linux.\n82\t- Starter comments and runtime config/gate settings share defaults in\n83\t  `src/config/defaults.ts`. Review flag defaults should use that module\n84\t  too, so starter guidance stays aligned with runtime behavior.\n85\t- Login orchestration shares `ctx.lines` across providers and prompts.\n86\t  Reuse `providersNeedingLogin` and `loginProvider` for login offers;\n87\t  `loginPath` owns the scope rules shared by login and logout.\n88\t\n89\t## Docs\n90\t\n91\t- User-facing docs (`README.md`, `docs/`, the bundled\n92\t  `internal/skill/assets/roast/SKILL.md`) write every invocation as\n93\t  `npx roast ...`; Roast is a project dependency, never a `PATH` binary.\n94\t  Settings are documented as `.roast.json` keys, never environment\n95\t  variables; only credentials, `ROAST_SKIP`, and test-only `ROAST_LIVE_*`\n96\t  / `ROAST_TEST_*` variables exist.\n97\t- CLI messages in `internal/cli` (for example the gate hint printed\n98\t  during review) still say bare `roast`; changing them is a code change,\n99\t  not a docs change.\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc9cd1ee-6217-41cc-8c13-e5fed07b92d5","uuid":"0fc2d900-72df-4cbf-a628-47ff257e42c9","timestamp":"2026-11-24T03:52:23.885Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-37-m6-cutover/AGENTS.md","content":"## Agent skills\n\n### Issue tracker\n\nIssues are tracked as local markdown files under `.scratch/`. See `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.\n\n### Triage labels\n\nDefault label vocabulary. See `docs/agents/triage-labels.md`.\n\n### Domain docs\n\nSingle-context layout. See `docs/agents/domain.md`.\n\n## Layout\n\nTwo implementations live side by side until the M6 cutover\n(`.scratch/ts-rewrite/`, ADR-0004): the Go CLI (`cmd/roast`,\n`internal/`) and its TypeScript rewrite (`src/`, `test/`, `scripts/`).\nBoth are under active change. `npm run test:go` runs the Go and launcher\ntests; `npm test` runs typecheck and the TS suite; lint is\n`npm run lint`.\n\n## Area notes\n\nBefore editing code in an area, read its notes. Each area file holds the\nGo and TS notes for that area side by side.\n\n- Any Go code or Go test: `docs/agents/go.md`\n- Any TS in `src/`, `test/`, or `scripts/`: `docs/agents/typescript.md`\n- Config loading, roles, providers, the `init` starter,\n  `roast.schema.json` (`internal/config`, `src/config/`):\n  `docs/agents/config.md`\n- Trust and approvals (`internal/trust`, `src/trust/`, `*/trust.*`):\n  `docs/agents/trust.md`\n- Stored credentials, `login`, `logout` (`internal/credentials`,\n  `src/credentials/`, `internal/cli/*login*`): `docs/agents/auth.md`\n- Gate and the pre-commit hook (`internal/gate`, `src/gate/`):\n  `docs/agents/gate.md`\n- Agent skill install (`internal/skill`, `src/skill/`):\n  `docs/agents/skill.md`\n- Run records (`internal/record`): `docs/agents/records.md`\n- Scope, context, exploration tools, snapshot denylist (`src/scope/`,\n  `src/context/`, `src/snapshot/`): `docs/agents/scope-context.md`\n- LLM adapters and the agent loop (`src/llm/`): `docs/agents/llm.md`\n- npm packaging, the launcher, release (`packages/`, `scripts/build.ts`,\n  `src/launcher.ts`): `docs/agents/packaging.md`\n\nA new note goes in its area's file; a new area gets a file and a line\nhere. This file holds only what most tasks hit.\n\n## Traps every task hits\n\n- `JSON.parse` syntax errors can quote the input. Credential-file parse\n  errors must use value-free messages so diagnostic output cannot expose\n  a stored key.\n- Shell hooks block Bash commands that contain a heredoc mentioning\n  `process.env.PATH`, a heredoc or command containing `env:` or `.env`\n  text, or a `credentials*` path together with `cat`, `sed`, `head`, and\n  the like. Read and write such files with the editor tools.\n- Tests that write project state (run records, trust, stored\n  credentials) chdir into a temporary Git repository first. `.roast/`\n  ignores itself, so a leak into this checkout is invisible to\n  `git status`; check with `ls -a`.\n- CLI diagnostic tests that resolve roles need valid test credentials\n  and local fake-server routing, even when asserting only local checks.\n  Doctor fakes must route GET models checks and POST inference separately;\n  a successful chat probe needs a lookup call followed by a final call\n  that echoes the token from the replayed tool result.\n- `.npmrc` sets `force=true` so npm links workspaces whose `os`/`cpu`\n  differ from the host. Expect \"using --force\" warnings from every npm\n  command.\n- The CLI parser preserves dashed option names and disables boolean\n  negation. Declare flags such as `no-browser` explicitly and read\n  `args['no-browser']`, rather than a camel-case property.\n- `simulateTerminals` only bypasses interactive-terminal detection. To\n  exercise raw-mode prompt input through the CLI, give stdin an `isTTY`\n  value of `true` and a `setRawMode` function; assert raw mode is restored.\n- Browser-login tests send callbacks with the real fetch; the injected\n  provider fetch rewrites every origin. Bound callback tests with\n  `loginTimeouts.browser` and set injected display variables on Linux.\n- Starter comments and runtime config/gate settings share defaults in\n  `src/config/defaults.ts`. Review flag defaults should use that module\n  too, so starter guidance stays aligned with runtime behavior.\n- Login orchestration shares `ctx.lines` across providers and prompts.\n  Reuse `providersNeedingLogin` and `loginProvider` for login offers;\n  `loginPath` owns the scope rules shared by login and logout.\n\n## Docs\n\n- User-facing docs (`README.md`, `docs/`, the bundled\n  `internal/skill/assets/roast/SKILL.md`) write every invocation as\n  `npx roast ...`; Roast is a project dependency, never a `PATH` binary.\n  Settings are documented as `.roast.json` keys, never environment\n  variables; only credentials, `ROAST_SKIP`, and test-only `ROAST_LIVE_*`\n  / `ROAST_TEST_*` variables exist.\n- CLI messages in `internal/cli` (for example the gate hint printed\n  during review) still say bare `roast`; changing them is a code change,\n  not a docs change.\n","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":100}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0154CLWsasdoN8zvhLj6aJYh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
