"-  `node_modules/.cache/roast-diff/` (delete it to force a rebuild).","-  Without `go` on `PATH` every scenario is a TAP skip.","-- Add a milestone's scenarios as a `Scenario[]` under","-  `test/diff/scenarios/` and list it in `SCENARIOS` (`index.ts`);","-  `server`, `records`, and `requests` turn on the fake server and","-  record/request comparison.","-- A difference caused by a deliberate change goes in `ALLOWLIST`","-  (`allowlist.ts`) naming the change number. Go behavior judged wrong","-  goes in the owning area's Open questions, never patched in the","-  harness.","-- Review scenarios are protocol-parametrized: `review(case, protocol)`","-  in `scenarios/m3.ts` names non-`chat` scenarios with a","-  ` (<protocol>)` suffix. M4 (`scenarios/m4.ts`) reruns the M3 cases on","-  `responses`, rewriting chat replies with `responsesFromChat`, and on","-  `anthropic`. Anthropic requests keep the system prompt out of","-  `messages` and merge consecutive user turns, so first calls key as","-  `<model>#1`.","-- Review scenarios script the fake with `scriptedServer` (`replies.ts`),","-  keyed by `<model>#<turns>` like the request groups. A first finder","-  call has 3 messages, a first verifier call 2; an unscripted key gets","-  a 404 naming it. Credential variables must not start with a scrubbed","-  prefix (`ROAST_`, `OPENAI_`, ...): `scrubbedEnv` drops them.","-- Go-only incidental bytes are normalized, not allowlisted: SDK headers","-  (`X-Stainless-*`), Go's `\\u003c` HTML escaping (records compare as","-  parsed JSON, including `provider-responses.jsonl`), gzip/zstd bytes","-  and the bundle-manifest hashes of compressed members, finding UUIDs","-  and aliases, and the snapshot `commit` / `ref` OIDs.","-- Self-tests that need a one-sided difference wrap the TS CLI: a node","-  script that edits records after `dist/cli.js` exits, or `node","-  --import <hook>` replacing `globalThis.fetch` (the adapters send a","-  `Uint8Array` body).","-- Multi-step scenarios list commands in `setup` (exit codes compared);","-  `argv` may be a function of the side's run IDs (oldest first), since","-  each side's run IDs differ. Run IDs have one-second resolution: pause","-  over a second between reviews so their order is deterministic.","-- Beyond stdout, a scenario can compare a side directory's file tree","-  (`tree`, with `absent` paths), refs under a prefix (`refs`, run IDs","-  replaced by position), and repository files (`written`, `.json`","-  parsed as JSONC). Snapshot ages follow `GIT_COMMITTER_DATE`, which a","-  setup step's `env` can override to age or future-date one snapshot.","-- Iterate on one self-test module without Go: `node scripts/bundle.ts","-  --test-file test/diff/selftest/<file>.ts && node test/one-bundle.js`","-  (needs `npm run build` for `dist/cli.js`)."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-37-m6-cutover/docs/agents/typescript.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016Xv4XgmVU49erdBneWvoM9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
