`npm pack --json` as an object keyed by package name,","   older npm as an array.","-- `npm run release` runs `scripts/check-release.ts` itself, after the","-  build and before `npm publish --workspaces`: platform packages have no","-  `prepublishOnly`, so the root hook alone would run too late.","-- `scripts/check-package.ts` is the post-M6 package check. It fails","-  against today's transitional manifest, so only its fixture tests","-  (`test/tooling/check-package.ts`) run it; keep it out of CI and npm","-  scripts until M6.","-","-## Tests","-","-- Launcher tests (`test/*.test.ts`, `node --test`) spawn the compiled","-  launcher from a temp fixture `node_modules` with a shell-script","-  binary, so they need `npm run build:launcher` first;","-  `npm run test:go` does this.","-- Release-script tests (`test/release-fixture.ts`) build a temp package","-  with the real root `scripts` and a symlink to `scripts/`, then run","-  `npm version` / `npm run prepublishOnly` there; `release.test.ts` puts","-  a logging fake `npm` first on `PATH`. None of them compile Go.","+- Release is local, through the npm lifecycle: `npm version <x>` runs","+  lint (`preversion`), updates the README toc and `CHANGELOG.md`","+  (`auto-changelog`), commits and tags, then `postversion` pushes and","+  publishes; `prepublishOnly` builds and runs `check:pack`. A failing","+  `prepublishOnly` after the tag is pushed is fixed by a follow-up patch","+  release, never by re-tagging."]}],"originalFile":"# npm packaging and release\n\n`src/launcher.ts`, `scripts/`, `packages/`. This is the Go-era layout;\nthe M6 cutover (`.scratch/ts-rewrite/issues/37-m6-cutover.md`) replaces\nit.\n\n## Layout\n\n- The root `bin` is `dist/launcher.js`, compiled from `src/launcher.ts`\n  by `npm run build:launcher`. It runs\n  `@substrate-system/roast-<platform>-<arch>/dist/roast[.exe]`; the six\n  platform packages live in `packages/` as npm workspaces.\n- `scripts/platforms.ts` is the single list of the six targets and\n  their package names and paths; `build.ts`, `version.ts` (`version`\n  lifecycle), `check-release.ts` (`prepublishOnly`) and `release.ts`\n  share it. All but `build.ts` operate on `process.cwd()` so tests can\n  run them in a fixture.\n- The root package has no `dependencies`: the launcher uses only Node\n  built-ins, and anything listed there installs into every user's\n  project.\n- There is no committed lockfile (`.npmrc` sets `package-lock=false`).\n  CI writes one with `npm install --package-lock-only\n  --package-lock=true` before `npm ci`, which refuses to run without it.\n\n## Building\n\n- `npm run build -- --host` builds only this machine's binary plus the\n  launcher. A full `npm run build` takes several minutes: it runs\n  `scripts/licenses.sh` once per target and copies the root\n  `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/` into each package's `dist/`.\n- `npx roast` in this repo resolves the root package's own bin, so build\n  first; a stale or non-executable `dist/launcher.js` lets a `roast` on\n  `PATH` (for example Homebrew) answer instead.\n\n## Checks and release\n\n- `npm run check:pack` (`scripts/check-pack.ts`, CI only) dry-run packs\n  every package and checks each tarball lists its `dist/` contents.\n  Changing a package's `files` or what `build.ts` writes into `dist/`\n  must keep it passing. It also requires Roast's own license files\n  (`LICENSES` in `scripts/platforms.ts`, copied into each platform\n  `dist/` by `build.ts`) and a `license` field in every manifest.\n- npm 12 prints `npm pack --json` as an object keyed by package name,\n  older npm as an array.\n- `npm run release` runs `scripts/check-release.ts` itself, after the\n  build and before `npm publish --workspaces`: platform packages have no\n  `prepublishOnly`, so the root hook alone would run too late.\n- `scripts/check-package.ts` is the post-M6 package check. It fails\n  against today's transitional manifest, so only its fixture tests\n  (`test/tooling/check-package.ts`) run it; keep it out of CI and npm\n  scripts until M6.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Launcher tests (`test/*.test.ts`, `node --test`) spawn the compiled\n  launcher from a temp fixture `node_modules` with a shell-script\n  binary, so they need `npm run build:launcher` first;\n  `npm run test:go` does this.\n- Release-script tests (`test/release-fixture.ts`) build a temp package\n  with the real root `scripts` and a symlink to `scripts/`, then run\n  `npm version` / `npm run prepublishOnly` there; `release.test.ts` puts\n  a logging fake `npm` first on `PATH`. None of them compile Go.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HW8Pw5Toj9Ta9TBVyZH1ij","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
