race`, so Go tests that spawn","-  `go` subprocesses inherit `-race`; such a subprocess must not also set","-  `CGO_ENABLED=0` for a build.","-","-## CLI tests (`internal/cli`)","-","-- Tests drive `ExecuteContext` against an `httptest` fake inference","-  server; `executeContext(ctx, args, stdin, stdout, stderr)` lets a test","-  answer prompts (`ExecuteContext` passes `os.Stdin`).","-- `internal/testutil.ClearAmbientEnvironment` strips `ROAST_*`,","-  `OPENAI_*`, `OPENROUTER_*` and `ANTHROPIC_*` in `TestMain`.","-- A test that runs a review needs a `.roast.json`","-  (`project_config_test.go`: `projectConfig`, `writeFile`, `chdir`,","-  `newModelRecorder`). Profiles name a credential with `api_key_env` and","-  set it with `t.Setenv`.","-- The `httptest` server is a custom endpoint, so a review test approves","-  first: `approveProjectConfig(t, ...)` (`trust_test.go`, runs","-  `trust --yes`), or `settingsRepo`, which approves. A test asserting a","-  config error approves a valid config and then edits it","-  (`approvedThenEdited`) so a trust failure cannot mask the error.","-- `roast doctor` skips endpoint probes for an unapproved config. A","-  doctor test that probes a custom endpoint chdirs into a temp repo and","-  approves there (`approveDoctorConfig`, `doctor_test.go`), never in","-  this checkout.","-- Untracked files are part of a review's diff, so a test that checks","-  which file's text reached the fake server keeps decoys out of scope","-  (for example via `.git/info/exclude`).","-- `settings_test.go` has `requestRecorder` (records model,","-  `Authorization`, body), `settingsRepo`, `reviewMeta` (reads the run's","-  `meta.json`), and `redirectDefaultTransport`, which swaps","-  `http.DefaultTransport` so a profile on a provider's default endpoint","-  reaches the fake server.","-- `init_test.go` has `providerServer`, a fake speaking the Responses","-  (`/v1/responses`), Anthropic (`/v1/messages`), and OpenRouter chat","-  (`/api/v1/chat/completions`) protocols; pair it with","-  `redirectDefaultTransport(t, server.URL)`.","-- Terminal detection goes through the package var","-  `interactiveTerminals` (`prompt.go`); tests swap it with","-  `simulateTerminals(t, ...)` (`trust_prompt_test.go`)."]}],"deleted":true},{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-37-m6-cutover/docs/agents/trust.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3,"newLines":7,"lines":[" Go: `internal/config/trust.go`, `internal/trust`, `internal/cli/trust.go`."," TS: `src/config/trust.ts`, `src/config/canonical.ts`,"," `src/trust/trust.ts`, `src/cli/trust.ts`. Design: ADR-0001, ADR-0003.","-How CLI tests approve a config is in `go.md`.","+How CLI tests approve a config is in `typescript.md`."," "," - `Config.TrustProjection()` is the security-relevant projection; its","   `Hash()` covers only endpoint, protocol, credential variable, and"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-37-m6-cutover/docs/agents/go.md","/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-37-m6-cutover/docs/agents/trust.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01U5F1D5XEjK2aM3bJMwydit","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
