standard key variable, key page, and login method","-  a provider has. Trust standardness, ambient credentials, and the","-  `init` starter consult it; add a provider there, not in those callers.","-  A provider's first protocol is the one starter profiles use.","-- A new provider's key variable also goes in `clearProviderEnv`","-  (`internal/config/credential_test.go`).","-- `DefaultBaseURL(protocol)` stays separate: it is the implicit endpoint","+- `lookupProvider(name)` and `providerAt(endpoint, protocol)`","+  (`provider.ts`) are the one place that says which endpoint,","+  protocols, standard key variable, key page, and login method a","+  provider has. Trust standardness, ambient credentials, and the `init`","+  starter consult it; add a provider there, not in those callers. A","+  provider's first protocol is the one starter profiles use.","+- A new provider's key variable must be stripped from test","+  environments: see `cleanEnv` in `typescript.md`.","+- `defaultBaseURL(protocol)` stays separate: it is the implicit endpoint","   of a profile that omits one; OpenRouter is never one."," - A role that gets no ambient key reports any set provider key variable","-  as `Withheld` (`withheldKey`), preferring the protocol's default","-  provider.","-- TS `provider.ts` `parseEndpoint` is the one endpoint parser (treats","-  `https:///v1` and `https:v1` as an empty host, like Go); `endpoint.ts`","-  and `sameEndpoint` use it.","+  as withheld (`withheldKey`, `credential.ts`), preferring the","+  protocol's default provider.","+- `parseEndpoint` (`provider.ts`) is the one endpoint parser (treats","+  `https:///v1` and `https:v1` as an empty host); `endpoint.ts` and","+  `sameEndpoint` use it."," ","-## TS roles (`role.ts`, `credential.ts`, `provider.ts`)","+## Roles (`role.ts`, `credential.ts`, `provider.ts`)"," "," - Resolution takes `env` explicitly and never reads `process.env`."," - `ResolvedRole` is frozen with a non-enumerable `apiKey` and `stored`,"]},{"oldStart":84,"oldLines":7,"newStart":79,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - `StoredCredentials` lives in `credential.ts` (re-exported by","   `load.ts`)."," ","-## TS tests","+## Tests"," "," - Role tests build configs with `configFrom` / `resolveFinder` and the","   in-memory `FakeStore` in `test/config/helpers.ts`."]}],"originalFile":"# Config, roles, and providers\n\nGo: `internal/config`, `internal/cli/config.go`. TS: `src/config/`,\n`src/cli/config.ts`. Credential lookup order is in `auth.md`.\n\n## Loading\n\n- Go `config.Load(path)` parses `.roast.json` as JSONC\n  (`hujson.Standardize`, then `encoding/json` with\n  `DisallowUnknownFields`). `version: 1` is required; a literal\n  `api_key` is rejected. There are no built-in roles or models: a role\n  missing from the config fails in `ResolveRole`.\n- TS `jsonc.ts` parses into null-prototype objects (`newObject` /\n  `setKey`, so `__proto__` is an ordinary key). `schema.ts` (zod) checks\n  shape and types only, and `load.ts` keeps the validated *input*, never\n  zod's output (zod's record output turns a `__proto__` key into a\n  prototype). Range and cross-field checks are plain functions in\n  `load.ts` so Go's check order holds.\n- `config.Find(start, stop)` walks up to `stop` (the Git toplevel),\n  comparing directories after `EvalSymlinks`: macOS temp dirs are\n  `/var/...` while `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` prints\n  `/private/var/...`.\n- The CLI loads config only through `loadProjectConfig` (Go also\n  `projectConfigPath`; TS `loadProjectConfig(explicit, ctx)`), which\n  attaches the stored-credentials store. A missing config is a usage\n  error naming `npx roast init`.\n- Relative prompt-override paths resolve against the config file's\n  directory: `config.Load` records it and callers read prompts through\n  `cfg.PromptPath(...)`, never the raw `cfg.Prompts.*` string. The trust\n  projection hashes the raw string, so approvals survive worktree moves.\n\n## Settings\n\nOnly credentials come from outside the config. Every other setting is\nin it (`limits`, `interactive`, `gate`, `review.snapshot`); optional\nnumbers are pointers so an explicit 0 differs from unset, and\n`validateSettings` checks ranges. Go `cli.go` resolves them with\n`flagOrConfigInt` / `flagOrConfigDuration` (flag, then config, then\ndefault).\n\n## Schema and starter\n\n- `roast.schema.json` (repo root, shipped through `package.json`\n  `files`) is generated: `npm run schema` renders\n  `src/config/json-schema.ts` from the zod schema. Adding, removing, or\n  retyping a config field changes `config.Config` and the zod schema in\n  the same change, then regenerates; never edit the JSON by hand.\n  `TestSchemaMatchesConfigStruct` (Go) and `test/config/schema.ts` fail\n  on drift. Editor-only constraints (enum, pattern, minimum, required)\n  go in the zod `.meta()`.\n- The `roast init` starter (`internal/config/starter.go`) shows\n  commented-out defaults that must track the defaults in\n  `internal/cli/cli.go`.\n- The starter places a model by its ID alone (`placeModel`): a\n  `<vendor>/<model>[:<variant>]` ID goes to OpenRouter, a bare ID to the\n  provider `InferFamily` names. A placeholder role follows an OpenRouter\n  role onto OpenRouter; otherwise it takes the other direct provider.\n\n## Providers\n\n- `LookupProvider(name)` and `ProviderAt(endpoint, protocol)`\n  (`internal/config/provider.go`) are the one place that says which\n  endpoint, protocols, standard key variable, key page, and login method\n  a provider has. Trust standardness, ambient credentials, and the\n  `init` starter consult it; add a provider there, not in those callers.\n  A provider's first protocol is the one starter profiles use.\n- A new provider's key variable also goes in `clearProviderEnv`\n  (`internal/config/credential_test.go`).\n- `DefaultBaseURL(protocol)` stays separate: it is the implicit endpoint\n  of a profile that omits one; OpenRouter is never one.\n- A role that gets no ambient key reports any set provider key variable\n  as `Withheld` (`withheldKey`), preferring the protocol's default\n  provider.\n- TS `provider.ts` `parseEndpoint` is the one endpoint parser (treats\n  `https:///v1` and `https:v1` as an empty host, like Go); `endpoint.ts`\n  and `sameEndpoint` use it.\n\n## TS roles (`role.ts`, `credential.ts`, `provider.ts`)\n\n- Resolution takes `env` explicitly and never reads `process.env`.\n- `ResolvedRole` is frozen with a non-enumerable `apiKey` and `stored`,\n  so JSON, spread, and `util.inspect` omit the secret. Change a role\n  with `updateRole(role, changes)`; a `{...role}` spread drops the key.\n- `StoredCredentials` lives in `credential.ts` (re-exported by\n  `load.ts`).\n\n## TS tests\n\n- Role tests build configs with `configFrom` / `resolveFinder` and the\n  in-memory `FakeStore` in `test/config/helpers.ts`.\n- Configs the tests load as realistic examples go in\n  `test/config/examples.ts`; the schema test validates each with ajv.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EqzwawRWcA7en4FCq7i9FV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
