{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KMvWnq4M5MrBizaKVYejW4","type":"tool_result","content":"# Roast\n\nAn adversarial, cross-model code reviewer. Install as a project dependency.\n\nA finder model proposes defects in a Git diff, each with a\ncode quote and a concrete fix. An independent verifier model then re-reads the\ncited code and confirms or refutes every claim before it reaches the report.\nThe two roles can use different providers, endpoints, and wire protocols.\n\nIn interactive mode, the models can navigate the local checkout\nvia read-only file, grep, and listing tools.\n\n<details><summary><h2>Contents</h2></summary>\n\n<!-- toc -->\n\n- [Fork](#fork)\n- [Quick start](#quick-start)\n  * [1. Install](#1-install)\n  * [2. Create the project config](#2-create-the-project-config)\n  * [3. Log in to your providers](#3-log-in-to-your-providers)\n  * [4. Review](#4-review)\n- [Install the agent skill](#install-the-agent-skill)\n- [Configure](#configure)\n  * [Project config](#project-config)\n  * [Credentials](#credentials)\n  * [Login and logout](#login-and-logout)\n  * [OpenRouter](#openrouter)\n  * [Command-line overrides](#command-line-overrides)\n  * [Author routes](#author-routes)\n  * [Other settings](#other-settings)\n- [Trust](#trust)\n- [Use](#use)\n- [Resource limits](#resource-limits)\n- [Exit codes](#exit-codes)\n- [Run records](#run-records)\n- [Pre-commit gate](#pre-commit-gate)\n- [Contributing](#contributing)\n- [License](#license)\n\n<!-- tocstop -->\n\n</details>\n\n## Fork\n\nThis is a fork of\n[bluesky-social/roast](https://github.com/bluesky-social/roast).\nThe fork adds `npm` ecosystem.\n\n\n## Quick start\n\nRoast runs in a Git repository with a `package.json`. It needs Node 20 or\nlater.\n\nThe [agent skill](#install-the-agent-skill) is optional.\nInstall it if you want a coding agent, such as Claude Code,\nto run reviews for you.\n\n### 1. Install\n\n```sh\nnpm i -D @substrate-system/roast\n```\n\n### 2. Create the project config\n\n```sh\nnpx roast init\n| --- | --- |\n| `gate.timeout_seconds` | Seconds before an unfinished review is stopped and the commit allowed. Default `180`; `0` disables. |\n| `gate.severity` | Lowest blocking severity: `INFO`, `LOW`, `MEDIUM`, `HIGH` (default), or `CRITICAL`. |\n| `gate.offer` | Whether the first interactive review offers to enable the gate. Default `true`. |\n| `ROAST_SKIP` | Environment variable. Any non-empty value (conventionally `1`) skips one commit. |\n\n## Contributing\n\nSee [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) for development checks and release\nsteps, and [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) to report a vulnerability.\n\n## License\n\nDual-licensed under [MIT](LICENSE-MIT.txt) or\n[Apache 2.0](LICENSE-APACHE.txt), at your option. Dependencies keep their own\nlicenses; CI checks the linked dependency graph against the allowed set.\n145:npx roast doctor\n149:`npx roast doctor` checks the config, credentials, and both endpoints with a\n181:package, so the installed copy matches the version you run.\n200:installed Roast version.\n218:  \"version\": 1,\n243:`version: 1` is required and unknown fields are rejected. `$schema` points\n297:`ROAST_VERIFIER_API_KEY`). `npx roast doctor` reports which source each role\n346:`chmod 600` it. `npx roast doctor` reports a credentials file that is too\n466:clone, delete `.git/roast/trust.json`. `npx roast doctor` reports whether the\n484:npx roast doctor","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc9cd1ee-6217-41cc-8c13-e5fed07b92d5","uuid":"3eedf474-c983-413d-b1d8-1930349f5db9","timestamp":"2026-11-24T03:55:12.604Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Roast\n\nAn adversarial, cross-model code reviewer. Install as a project dependency.\n\nA finder model proposes defects in a Git diff, each with a\ncode quote and a concrete fix. An independent verifier model then re-reads the\ncited code and confirms or refutes every claim before it reaches the report.\nThe two roles can use different providers, endpoints, and wire protocols.\n\nIn interactive mode, the models can navigate the local checkout\nvia read-only file, grep, and listing tools.\n\n<details><summary><h2>Contents</h2></summary>\n\n<!-- toc -->\n\n- [Fork](#fork)\n- [Quick start](#quick-start)\n  * [1. Install](#1-install)\n  * [2. Create the project config](#2-create-the-project-config)\n  * [3. Log in to your providers](#3-log-in-to-your-providers)\n  * [4. Review](#4-review)\n- [Install the agent skill](#install-the-agent-skill)\n- [Configure](#configure)\n  * [Project config](#project-config)\n  * [Credentials](#credentials)\n  * [Login and logout](#login-and-logout)\n  * [OpenRouter](#openrouter)\n  * [Command-line overrides](#command-line-overrides)\n  * [Author routes](#author-routes)\n  * [Other settings](#other-settings)\n- [Trust](#trust)\n- [Use](#use)\n- [Resource limits](#resource-limits)\n- [Exit codes](#exit-codes)\n- [Run records](#run-records)\n- [Pre-commit gate](#pre-commit-gate)\n- [Contributing](#contributing)\n- [License](#license)\n\n<!-- tocstop -->\n\n</details>\n\n## Fork\n\nThis is a fork of\n[bluesky-social/roast](https://github.com/bluesky-social/roast).\nThe fork adds `npm` ecosystem.\n\n\n## Quick start\n\nRoast runs in a Git repository with a `package.json`. It needs Node 20 or\nlater.\n\nThe [agent skill](#install-the-agent-skill) is optional.\nInstall it if you want a coding agent, such as Claude Code,\nto run reviews for you.\n\n### 1. Install\n\n```sh\nnpm i -D @substrate-system/roast\n```\n\n### 2. Create the project config\n\n```sh\nnpx roast init\n| --- | --- |\n| `gate.timeout_seconds` | Seconds before an unfinished review is stopped and the commit allowed. Default `180`; `0` disables. |\n| `gate.severity` | Lowest blocking severity: `INFO`, `LOW`, `MEDIUM`, `HIGH` (default), or `CRITICAL`. |\n| `gate.offer` | Whether the first interactive review offers to enable the gate. Default `true`. |\n| `ROAST_SKIP` | Environment variable. Any non-emp