{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChM5WBZRCp2j8t4p6YpFA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WiKCcnbKYnXhLjGxongerD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'; s=open(p).read()\nrep=[(\"\"\"Roast runs in a Git repository with a `package.json`. It needs Node 20 or\nlater.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"Roast runs in a Git repository with a `package.json`. It needs Node 22.18\nor later on macOS or Linux; Windows is not supported. Roast is pure\nJavaScript: one bundled file with no prebuilt binaries and no Go\ntoolchain, and installing it adds no other packages to your project.\n\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"```sh\nnpm i -D @substrate-system/roast\n```\n\"\"\",\"\"\"```sh\nnpm i -D @substrate-system/roast\n```\n\n`npx roast --version` prints the installed version, commit, and build\ndate.\n\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"The `limits` and `gate` sections are described under\n[Resource limits](#resource-limits) and [Pre-commit gate](#pre-commit-gate).\n`npx roast init` writes them as commented-out defaults.\n\nRuns record the profile name and resolved non-secret settings, never API keys.\nThe invocation argv is recorded, so keep secrets out of command-line values.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"The `limits` and `gate` sections are described under\n[Resource limits](#resource-limits) and [Pre-commit gate](#pre-commit-gate).\n`npx roast init` writes them as commented-out defaults.\n\nRuns record the profile name and resolved non-secret settings, never API keys.\nThe invocation argv is recorded, so keep secrets out of command-line values.\n\n### Network\n\nRoast uses Node's built-in `fetch` and bundles no proxy library. Behind\na proxy, set `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1` so Node honors `HTTPS_PROXY`,\n`HTTP_PROXY`, and `NO_PROXY`; without it those variables are ignored,\nand `npx roast doctor` warns when `HTTPS_PROXY` is set alone. For a\nprivate or corporate certificate authority, point\n`NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS` at a PEM file holding its certificate:\n\n```sh\nexport NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1\nexport HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.example.com:8080\nexport NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/etc/ssl/certs/corporate-ca.pem\nnpx roast review\n```\n\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"  * [Other settings](#other-settings)\n\"\"\",\"\"\"  * [Other settings](#other-settings)\n  * [Network](#network)\n\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"Dual-licensed under [MIT](LICENSE-MIT.txt) or\n[Apache 2.0](LICENSE-APACHE.txt), at your option. Dependencies keep their own\nlicenses; CI checks the linked dependency graph against the allowed set.\"\"\",\"\"\"Dual-licensed under [MIT](LICENSE-MIT.txt) or\n[Apache 2.0](LICENSE-APACHE.txt), at your option. Bundled libraries keep\ntheir own licenses: the build checks each against an allowed set and ships\ntheir notices in `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`.\"\"\"),\n]\nfor a,b in rep:\n    assert a in s, a[:50]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n -i \"go\\b\\|golang\\|platform pack\\|binary\\|launcher\\|windows\\|20 or\" README.md | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1106,"cache_read_input_tokens":203338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1106},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc9cd1ee-6217-41cc-8c13-e5fed07b92d5","uuid":"6b67c97e-0def-47d6-a95b-988cb63b4275","timestamp":"2026-11-24T03:55:26.419Z","request_id":"req_011ChM5WBPVMhe2PZ8RsswFL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WiKCcnbKYnXhLjGxongerD":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-37-m6-cutover && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'; s=open(p).read()\nrep=[(\"\"\"Roast runs in a Git repository with a `package.json`. It needs Node 20 or\nlater.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"Roast runs in a Git repository with a `package.json`. It needs Node 22.1