 no build, a","+`roast` elsewhere on your `PATH` can answer instead."," "," Also run these before opening a pull request:"," "," ```sh","-go vet ./...","-go tool -modfile=.github/tools/staticcheck/go.mod staticcheck ./...","-go tool -modfile=.github/tools/actionlint/go.mod actionlint","-shellcheck scripts/*.sh","+npm run check:pack","+go -C .github/tools/actionlint tool actionlint","+shellcheck src/gate/pre-commit.sh"," ```"," ","-CI-only Go tools have separate modules under `.github/tools/`, maintained by","-Renovate without adding them to Roast's runtime dependencies. Use those modules","-locally too; a separately installed version can have a different Go importer.","+`npm run check:pack` dry-run packs the package and checks that the","+tarball holds the bundle, its notices, the schema, and Roast's license","+files, and that the manifest declares no dependencies. CI-only Go tools","+have separate modules under `.github/tools/`, maintained by Renovate."," ","-Format Go changes with `gofmt`. Tests use local HTTP servers and temporary Git","-repositories; they must not require real model credentials or send repository","-content to an inference provider.","+Tests use local HTTP servers and temporary Git repositories; they must","+not require real model credentials or send repository content to an","+inference provider."," ","-Opt-in live tests in `internal/llm` run a minimal two-turn tool loop (one","-exploration call, its result, then the submission on the wrap-up turn) against","-a real endpoint with a small output ceiling. They send a fixed probe prompt,","-never repository content, and skip unless their API key variable is set:","+Opt-in live tests in `test/live/` run a minimal two-turn tool loop (one","+exploration call, its result, then the submission on the wrap-up turn)","+against a real endpoint with a small output ceiling. They send a fixed","+probe prompt, never repository content, and skip unless their API key","+variable is set. `npm test` never runs them, and neither does CI:"," "," | Variable | Default |"," | --- | --- |"]},{"oldStart":78,"oldLines":27,"newStart":67,"newLines":20,"lines":[" | `ROAST_LIVE_DEEPSEEK_PROTOCOL` | `chat` (or `anthropic` with an `/anthropic/v1` base URL) |"," "," ```sh","-ROAST_LIVE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=... go test ./internal/llm -run TestLive -count=1 -v","+ROAST_LIVE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=... npm run test:live"," ```"," ","-With a DeepSeek key, a second test makes one structured call with a 256-token","-output ceiling, which a thinking model spends on reasoning before it calls a","-tool. It checks that the error names the `length` finish and suggests raising","-`max_output_tokens`, and skips if the model answers within the ceiling.","-","-The Anthropic test also sends the `thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01` beta","-header without changing the mismatch behavior, so accounts that do not enforce","-thinking-block binding still report a replay whose prefix changed; the test","-fails on any such report. Tests read these variables before clearing the","-ambient environment, so other tests never see them. Never commit keys or paste","-them into logs.","-","-Before opening a pull request, also check that `go mod tidy` leaves `go.mod`","-and `go.sum` unchanged, including the tool modules (run `go mod tidy` inside","-each tool directory). CI runs vulnerability, Git-history secret, and","-dependency-license checks. New runtime dependencies must use a license","-compatible with Roast's MIT/Apache-2.0 dual license and should be justified in","-the pull request.","+With a DeepSeek key, a second test makes one structured call with a","+256-token output ceiling, which a thinking model spends on reasoning","+before it calls a tool. It checks that the error names the `length`","+finish and suggests raising `max_output_tokens`, and skips if the model","+answers within the ceiling. Never commit keys or paste them into logs.","+","+CI runs a Git-history secret scan and `npm audit --audit-level=high`.","+Roast has no runtime `dependencies`: libraries it runs are","+`devDependencies` bundled into `dist/cli.js`. A new bundled library","+must use a license on the allowlist (see \"Third-party notices\" below)","+and should be justified in the pull request."," "," Pull-request CI runs on GitHub-hosted runners with read-only repository"," permissions and no inference or publishing credentials. The `claude-review`"]},{"oldStart":121,"oldLines":47,"newStart":103,"newLines":38,"lines":[" ## Releases"," "," Roast is published to npm only, from a maintainer's machine; CI never","-publishes. The root package `@substrate-system/roast` holds the launcher and","-the config schema, and the six `@substrate-system/roast-<os>-<arch>` packages","-each hold one binary and its license notices.","+publishes. `@substrate-system/roast` is one package holding","+`dist/cli.js`, its third-party notices, the config schema, and Roast's","+license files."," "," ```sh","-npm version <new-version>","-npm run release","+npm version <major|minor|patch|x.y.z>"," ```"," ","-`npm version` runs the `version` lifecycle script, which writes the new","-version into every platform package and into the root package's","-`optionalDependencies`, so the version commit includes them all.","-`npm run release` runs `npm run build`, publishes the platform packages","-through the workspaces, then publishes the root package. Extra arguments","-(such as `--dry-run`) go to both publish steps. The root package's","-`prepublishOnly` refuses to publish unless all six binaries and their license","-notices exist and every version matches.","-","-## Dependency notices","-","-`bash scripts/licenses.sh [<goos>/<goarch> ...]` checks and collects runtime","-dependency licenses and notices for the CGO-disabled release targets (all six","-by default). It uses the `go-licenses/v2` tool module in","-`.github/tools/licenses`, generates per-target CSV inventories, and includes","-the Go runtime/standard-library license. Generated files live in the ignored","-`THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/` directory, separate from Roast's own licenses. The","-script refuses to replace a directory it did not generate, and failed","-generation leaves any previous bundle intact.","-","-`npm run build` runs the script once per target and copies that target's","-notices into its platform package's `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/`. When a","-dependency drops out of the `./cmd/roast` graph, check","-`go list -deps ./cmd/roast` for each target and update any notice the script","-special-cases. When changing dependencies, inspect the generated inventories;","-automated classification is not a substitute for legal review.","-","-Prefer tagged stable dependency releases. Explain any necessary development pin","-or prerelease in its pull request and revisit it when a stable release permits.","-Rerun provider tests, module checks, vulnerability checks, and notice generation","-after dependency changes; old advisory notes are not a substitute for scanning","-the selected module graph.","+The npm lifecycle does the rest. `preversion` runs `npm run lint`; npm","+writes the version into `package.json`; `version` updates the README","+table of contents and `CHANGELOG.md` (through `auto-changelog`) and","+stages them; npm commits and tags `v<x.y.z>`; `postversion` pushes the","+commit and tag and runs `npm publish`, whose `prepublishOnly` runs","+`npm run build` and `npm run check:pack`. If `prepublishOnly` fails","+after the tag was pushed, fix it with a follow-up patch release rather","+than re-tagging.","+","+## Third-party notices","+","+`npm run build` writes `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt` from the esbuild","+metafile (`scripts/licenses.ts`): one entry per package that has code in","+the bundle, with its declared license and the license files it ships.","+The build fails, naming the package, when a bundled package has no","+`license` field, no license file, or a license outside the allowlist","+`Apache-2.0`, `BSD-2-Clause`, `BSD-3-Clause`, `ISC`, `MIT`, `MPL-2.0`,","+`Unlicense`. Extending the allowlist needs maintainer approval. When","+changing dependencies, read the generated notices; automated","+classification is not a substitute for legal review.","+","+Prefer tagged stable dependency releases. Explain any necessary","+development pin or prerelease in its pull request and revisit it when a","+stable release permits."," "," ## Security"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-37-m6-cutover/CONTRIBUTING.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CmUTah8i8pcsV2Rqudtk5q","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
