{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChM5uZURvztqkh9Gm5Ztu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `git ls-files` lists no `*.go`, `go.mod`, `go.sum`, `packages/`, `src/launcher.ts`, or `test/diff/` path. The 12 templates, `SKILL.md`, and `pre-commit.sh` exist only under `src/`, and git shows them as renames.\n[x] The text-asset tests pass against the new locations. Each asset imported through the loader equals its file on disk.\n[x] `package.json` deep-equals the 2.1 manifest apart from `version`, which stays at its pre-release value, and dependency version ranges current at the time. It has no `dependencies`, `optionalDependencies`, `workspaces`, `main`, or `exports`.\n[x] `.npmrc` is exactly `package-lock=false`, and `.gitignore` has no Go-era entries.\n[x] `npm install` in a clean clone prints no \"using --force\" warning.\n[x] `npm pack --dry-run --json` lists exactly the `files` from 2.1. `npm run check:pack` (the renamed slim check) passes.\n[x] Installing the packed tarball into an empty temp project adds no transitive packages. `npx roast --version` there exits 0.\n[x] `ci.yml` has no Go setup in the test job, no gofmt, vet, staticcheck, govulncheck, or go-licenses step, and no harness job. The security job runs gitleaks, actionlint, `npm audit --audit-level=high`, and `shellcheck src/gate/pre-commit.sh`. `actionlint` passes on it.\n[x] AGENTS.md, `docs/agents/`, README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, and the review prompt contain no reference to `internal/`, `go test`, `go mod tidy`, staticcheck, `GOFLAGS`, platform packages, or the launcher.\n[x] The final-state CI steps pass locally on this machine: `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `git diff --exit-code -- roast.schema.json`, and `npm run check:pack`.\n\nThe M6 cutover is finished. The repository is now one TypeScript package and every final CI step passes locally: lint, typecheck, `npm test` (7513/7513), the schema diff, and `check:pack`. Everything is committed; only `.redeye/notes.md` is left out, as instructed.\n\n**Preconditions to put in the PR:**\n- **Test plans:** green at the final commit.\n- **Build and package check:** both pass against the final manifest.\n- **Differential harness:** not a clean pass. Exit codes, JSON output and run records match Go in every scenario. 24 scenarios still differ only because TS sends the `__roast_continue` nudge tool and Go never does. That is spec 07 Open question 1, which is still undecided. I counted that as meeting \"each difference is an accepted Open question\", but the PR should say plainly that the decision is still open.\n- **My mistake during the harness run:** I deleted the harness's Go binary cache while the first run was still going, which spoiled it. I reran it from a pre-cutover checkout, and that second run is the one reported above.\n\n**Things you may not expect:**\n- **New `overrides` key:** a clean `npm install` failed without `force`, because typescript-eslint only accepts TypeScript below 6.1 and we use 7. The old `force=true` was hiding this, and CI's install would have failed the same way. I added `\"overrides\": { \"typescript\": \"$typescript\" }` to `package.json`, and a clean clone now installs with no force warning and lints cleanly.\n- **Your shell sets `npm_config_force`:** that is why the \"using --force\" warning kept showing locally after the repo stopped setting it. I recorded this in `docs/agents/packaging.md`.\n- **Manifest is not an exact match for 2.1:** besides the override, I kept a few things the repo still needs:\n  - the TypeScript 6 lint shim and `@typescript/typescript6`\n  - `ajv`, used by the schema test\n  - the `test:one` script\n  - the `.pi/` tooling packages\n  - `allowScripts`\n- **CI Go tools:** with no root `go.mod`, `go tool -modfile=...` no longer works. gitleaks and actionlint now run as `go -C .github/tools/<tool> tool <tool>`; I checked both locally.\n- **Deleted `capture.go`:** `test/runbundle/fixtures/capture.go` was the last tracked Go file and can't run without the deleted Go code. Its README now says the fixtures are frozen.\n- **Tarball contents:** `npm pack` lists the six `files` plus `README.md` and `package.json`, which npm always adds.\n- **`npm test` no longer typechecks:** that follows spec 2.1, so run `npm run typecheck` separately.\n\nThe `2.0.0` release and deprecating the old platform packages are left for ticket 38."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":416,"cache_read_input_tokens":230755,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":416},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc9cd1ee-6217-41cc-8c13-e5fed07b92d5","uuid":"734ca44f-4589-477a-95a8-e18bac40c588","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:00:48.086Z","request_id":"req_011ChM5uZJ1uQE3NcsQd6iVL"}
